## Sanity check: size of the losses

An uncalibrated simulator can easily produce implausible losses, so we check the scale against an assumed AUM of $5.0B. Expected annual incurred loss (all events, discovered or not) over 200 simulated databases:


::: {#tbl-scale .cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
sims <- parallel::mclapply(1:200, \(r) {
  simulate_database(base, rep = r) |>
    summarise(inc = sum(severity) / (params$horizon$n_origin / 4), n = n() / (params$horizon$n_origin / 4), .by = type)
}, mc.cores = max(1L, parallel::detectCores() - 2L)) |>
  bind_rows(.id = "rep")
by_type <- sims |>
  summarise(`Mean loss / yr` = mean(inc), `Events / yr` = mean(n), .by = type) |>
  mutate(Type = type_lab[type], `bps of AUM` = `Mean loss / yr` / aum * 1e4)
total <- sims |> summarise(inc = sum(inc), .by = rep)
bind_rows(
  by_type |> select(Type, `Events / yr`, `Mean loss / yr`, `bps of AUM`),
  tibble(Type = "All types", `Events / yr` = sum(by_type$`Events / yr`), `Mean loss / yr` = mean(total$inc), `bps of AUM` = mean(total$inc) / aum * 1e4)
) |>
  gt::gt() |>
  gt::fmt_number(c(`Events / yr`, `bps of AUM`), decimals = 1) |>
  gt::fmt_currency(`Mean loss / yr`, decimals = 0) |>
  gt::tab_source_note(sprintf("Annual total: median %.1f bps, 95th percentile %.1f bps of AUM. Targeted range: 10-15 bps mean; this is an assumption, not a benchmark.", median(total$inc) / aum * 1e4, quantile(total$inc, .95) / aum * 1e4))
```

